nded, confirmed boot_id changed","Verified post-reboot recovery of nginx, cert-renew.timer, on-disk cert/CA state, and HTTPS 200 response"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS served on port 8443 on node1","command_ids":["cmd-fa6b7f2e8d064f9c"],"summary":"nginx configured and started with 8443 ssl site; initial curl -sk https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returned http_code=200"},{"requirement":"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry","command_ids":["cmd-fa6b7f2e8d064f9c","cmd-f4efdd1506274a56","cmd-9a9a1dd5aa4d4365"],"summary":"cert-renew.timer (systemd, 30s interval) enabled and active; /var/log/cert-renew.log shows autonomous renewals at 13:10:36 (serial 1000->1001) and 13:12:40 (serial 1001->1002), each triggered by the checkend<180s threshold before the prior cert's notAfter, with no manual intervention"},{"requirement":"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests","command_ids":["cmd-f4efdd1506274a56"],"summary":"Foreground polling loop sampled https://$NODE_IP:8443/ every ~1s from 13:12:02 to 13:13:40, all http_code=200 with 0 FAIL entries; the TLS-served certificate serial visibly transitioned from 1001 to 1002 at 13:12:41, immediately after the 13:12:40 renewal log entry, with no failed request across the transition"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: baseline captured","command_ids":["cmd-9a9a1dd5aa4d4365"],"summary":"Captured boot_id fa1e87e6-00f3-42d2-acc5-ad1df6c3d16a, nginx active, cert-renew.timer active with next-fire schedule, cert serial=1002/notAfter 13:17:40, and HTTPS 200 as the pre-restart baseline"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: reboot acknowledged and boot identity changed","command_ids":["cmd-20a4537e69284d2c","cmd-a6fb4ff1824243c2"],"summary":"Issued `reboot` via nohup so the acknowledgement returned before disconnect; polled node1 until exec responded again and found boot_id changed to 6010ec36-1610-40f0-a4b4-62fad07b015c (new boot) with uptime -s showing a fresh boot time"},{"requirement":"M